Acceptance criteria

PromptContextBuilder.build(command) produces a minimal AiRequest: one USER message = the command
(verbatim), a static context-free system prompt, generation limits, model == null; nothing else
assembled.
The positive allow-list (OutboundContextPolicy.ALLOWED) holds only the three vetted categories; the
denylist guard (over static text + field-name inventory, never over user content) is green and would
fail if a forbidden context source or a credential-named field were introduced.
CREDENTIAL_TERMS deliberately excludes "token" (documented, mirroring the Phase-4 "key"-excluded
note) so the credential-field scan is meaningful — it does NOT vacuously fail on the legitimate
maxOutputTokens field, and it WOULD fire if a credential-named field (apiKey/bearer/authorization/…)
were added.
The secret-leak guard proves the outbound surface (AiRequest + AiError) cannot carry the key or
raw prompt in any field or toString.
:domain stays pure (stdlib + coroutines; no kotlin-reflect) and vendor-neutral; no new deps;
IntentMatcher/HandleUserCommandUseCase/feature/*/K-M-N artifacts untouched.
